{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>Who can count</b> — its meaning is: who placed them like a sapphire, as in the sense of: כראי מוצק [like a molten mirror]. Some say it is from ספר [book/count]. Others said: from מספר [number]. Others said: מי יספר בחכמתו [who counts in His wisdom] the skies." "<b>And the bottles of heaven</b> — they are the clouds, because they are full of water." "<b>Can cause to lie down</b> — like 'causes to descend,' and similar to it: שכבת הטל [the lying down of the dew]."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:05:09.148667177Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}